<!DOCTYPE gsdoc PUBLIC "-//GNUstep//DTD gsdoc 1.0.4//EN" "http://www.gnustep.org/gsdoc-1_0_4.dtd">
<gsdoc base="TTIOImporterRegistry" stylesheeturl="default-styles.css">
  <head>
    <title>TTIOImporterRegistry documentation</title>
    <author name="Generated by "></author>
    <date>Generated at 2026-06-05</date>
  </head>
  <body>
    <front><contents /></front>
    <chapter>
      <heading>
        Software documentation for the TTIOImporterFormatSpec
        class
      </heading>
      <class name="TTIOImporterFormatSpec" super="NSObject">
        <declared>TTIOImporterRegistry.h</declared>
        <desc>
          <p>
            <em>Declared In:</em> Import/TTIOImporterRegistry.h
          </p>
          <p>
            One immutable entry in the importer registry: a
            canonical format key paired with its GUI display
            name, file extensions, the external tool it shells
            out to (or <code>nil</code>), and the
            <code>TTIOReader</code> instance that parses inputs
            into a <code>TTIOImportedDataset</code>.
          </p>
          <p>
            Mirrors Python
            <code>ttio.importers.registry.FormatSpec</code> and
            Java
            <code>
              global.thalion.ttio.importers.ImporterRegistry.FormatSpec
            </code>
            .
          </p>
        </desc>
        <method type="NSString*">
          <sel>displayName</sel>
          <desc>
            Getter for property 'displayName' with attributes
            (nonatomic, readonly, copy).
          </desc>
        </method>
        <method type="NSArray*">
          <sel>extensions</sel>
          <desc>
            Getter for property 'extensions' with attributes
            (nonatomic, readonly, copy).
          </desc>
        </method>
        <method type="NSString*">
          <sel>key</sel>
          <desc>
            Getter for property 'key' with attributes
            (nonatomic, readonly, copy).
          </desc>
        </method>
        <method type="id&lt;TTIOReader&gt;">
          <sel>reader</sel>
          <desc>
            Getter for property 'reader' with attributes
            (strong, nonatomic, readonly).
          </desc>
        </method>
      </class>
    </chapter>
    <chapter>
      <heading>
        Software documentation for the TTIOImporterRegistry
        class
      </heading>
      <class name="TTIOImporterRegistry" super="NSObject">
        <declared>TTIOImporterRegistry.h</declared>
        <desc>
          <p>
            <em>Declared In:</em> Import/TTIOImporterRegistry.h
          </p>
          <p>
            Encode-format registry: the single source of
            truth for the formats
            <code>ttio encode --format &lt;fmt&gt;</code>
            accepts and how each maps to a <code>.tio</code>.
            Mirrors the Python
            <code>ttio.importers.registry</code> module and the
            merged Java <code>ImporterRegistry</code>; the
            canonical key set, alias table and CLI-delegated
            formats are fenced for byte-parity across
            languages.
          </p>
          <p>
            <code>fasta</code> / <code>fastq</code> are
            intentionally NOT registered here: they keep
            their richer dedicated CLIs and are exposed via
            <code>
              <ref type="method" id="+supportedEncodeFormats">
                +supportedEncodeFormats
              </ref>
            </code>
            only (CLI_DELEGATED).
          </p>
        </desc>
        <method type="BOOL" factory="yes">
          <sel>encodeFormat:</sel>
          <arg type="NSString*">format</arg>
          <sel>inputs:</sel>
          <arg type="NSArray&lt;NSString*&gt;*">inputs</arg>
          <sel>output:</sel>
          <arg type="NSString*">output</arg>
          <sel>options:</sel>
          <arg type="NSDictionary&lt;NSString*,id&gt;*">options</arg>
          <sel>error:</sel>
          <arg type="NSError*_Nullable*_Nullable">error</arg>
          <desc>
            Dispatches <code><var>inputs</var></code>
            &#8594; <code><var>output</var></code>
            <code>.tio</code> for a registry format:
            <code>
              [[spec.reader readInputs:...]
              writeToPath:output]
            </code>
            . @return <code>YES</code> on success; <code>NO</code> +
            <var>error</var> for an unknown <var>format</var> or
            a reader/write failure.
          </desc>
        </method>
        <method type="BOOL" factory="yes">
          <sel>isRegistryFormat:</sel>
          <arg type="NSString*">format</arg>
          <desc>
            <code>YES</code> if the (normalised)
            <var>format</var> is a registry key.
          </desc>
        </method>
        <method type="NSString*" factory="yes">
          <sel>normalizeFormat:</sel>
          <arg type="NSString*">format</arg>
          <desc>
            Canonicalises a user token: lowercase + trim
            + alias-map.
          </desc>
        </method>
        <method type="NSArray&lt;NSString*&gt;*" factory="yes">
          <sel>registryKeys</sel>
          <desc>
            The canonical registry keys, sorted ascending.
          </desc>
        </method>
        <method type="TTIOImporterFormatSpec*" factory="yes">
          <sel>specForFormat:</sel>
          <arg type="NSString*">format</arg>
          <sel>error:</sel>
          <arg type="NSError*_Nullable*_Nullable">error</arg>
          <desc>
            The spec for a <var>format</var>, or <code>nil</code> +
            <var>error</var> if unknown.
          </desc>
        </method>
        <method type="NSArray&lt;NSString*&gt;*" factory="yes">
          <sel>supportedEncodeFormats</sel>
          <desc>
            All formats <code>encode</code> accepts: registry keys
            ∪ CLI_DELEGATED, sorted.
          </desc>
        </method>
      </class>
    </chapter>
  </body>
</gsdoc>
